the deadlines, a second each:
  a connection that sends nothing: closed, 0 bytes
  HTTP/1.1 200 OK
  Content-Type: text/plain; charset=utf-8
  Content-Length: 6
  | hello
  then idle: the server closes, read gives 0 bytes
  a head that stops half way:
  HTTP/1.1 408 Request Timeout
  Content-Type: text/plain; charset=utf-8
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Content-Length: 20
  Connection: close
  | 408 Request Timeout
  | 
  a body that stops half way:
  HTTP/1.1 408 Request Timeout
  Content-Type: text/plain; charset=utf-8
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Content-Length: 20
  Connection: close
  | body read timed out
  | 
  32 MiB answered to a client that reads nothing for 3 s: cut short 1
a multipart upload:
  HTTP/1.1 200 OK
  Content-Type: text/plain; charset=utf-8
  Content-Length: 235
  Connection: close
  | part name=[title] file=[] type=[] 7 bytes sha256 e6c308a66dd78ad1
  | part name=[doc] file=[informe.pdf] type=[application/pdf] 300000 bytes sha256 f6cd5f2bbfef209a
  | part name=[note] file=[año.txt] type=[] 42 bytes sha256 806faa532c41cfb7
  | 
  the file sent: sha256 f6cd5f2bbfef209a; the last part's: 806faa532c41cfb7
